into the Bay Area and out to global markets</h2><p>Supported by Guangzhou’s location and logistics network, the show will welcome professional buyers and industry resources from Southeast Asian markets including Thailand, Vietnam, Malaysia, the Philippines, and Singapore. It will also bring together quality Chinese businesses with export capabilities, connecting Chinese brands with ASEAN channels and new growth across Asia.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Precise matching that supports trade</h2><p>Professional business matching is central to the show. Purchase-demand matching, buyer invitations, and on-site meetings give exhibitors direct access to buyers and channel partners with clear commercial interest, reducing the cost of communication and qualification while turning brand exposure into orders and long-term partnerships.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>One-stop sourcing and consumer insight</h2><p>The show brings together snacks, health foods, trend-led beverages, specialty ingredients, and other categories, spanning source manufacturers, established brands, and innovative businesses. Professional visitors can efficiently identify suppliers with cost and innovation advantages while observing real market feedback from South China to inform sourcing and market planning.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>LuxurEat (露意膳) connects new partnership opportunities</h2><p>LuxurEat (露意膳) will present TruffleEat, CaviarEat, Ugolini, and other brands, showcasing truffles, caviar, and premium gourmet products. We look forward to connecting with distributors, foodservice businesses, sourcing platforms, and international partners to expand further across China and Asia.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Admission notice</h2><p>This is a professional food and beverage trade show open only to industry professionals. Visitors under 18 years old and non-professional visitors aged 70 or above are not permitted to enter.</p></section><blockquote class="lux-reader-quote">Connecting the Greater Bay Area with Asian markets and new opportunities in premium food.</blockquote></div></section></article></main>
